  {
   "id": "verseText",
   "type": "inscription",
   "style": "plaque",
   "wall": [
    [
     33,
     56
    ],
    "n"
   ],
   "caption": "A bronze plaque beside the door",
   "title": "To whoever comes with a light",
   "sig": "Ilvaris, who eats candles",
   "pages": [
    "Thief, you have brought me a light. Good. I have been so hungry.\n\nWhere my bearers kneel, the masons’ road shows only to those who dim their own.\n\nWhere my eyes sleep, keep them sleeping. Go as the blind go: by pole, and by patience.\n\nMy bells remember the order of their making. Ring them as they were cast.\n\nMy hall breathes fire. Cross it while it draws breath.",
    "Give your flame to the hook, and let the mirrors carry it to the sun.\n\nWhat I loved, I kept in humble wood.\n\nThere is a road across my gulf. Your lantern lies about it.\n\nThree faces guard my sleep. Weep not, laugh not. Dream.\n\nAnd when at last you find me, bring fire. In the dark I am only smoke."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "stairText",
   "type": "inscription",
   "style": "look",
   "wall": [
    [
     34,
     60
    ],
    "s"
   ],
   "caption": "The stair you came down",
   "title": "Sealed",
   "pages": [
    "The stair-slab ground shut the moment your feet left the last step. There is no seam you can find, no ring to pull. The only way left is in."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "steleText",
   "type": "inscription",
   "style": "stele",
   "pos": [
    87900,
    126200
   ],
   "caption": "A stele at the foot of the hall",
   "title": "The Kneeling Bearers",
   "pages": [
    "Here kneel the lamp-bearers of Gloamhollow, who gave their lights to the Lady and keep their bowls empty in her honour.\n\nThe masons who laid this floor walked home each evening by their own marks. The marks are faint.\n\nYour light is loud."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "scrawlText",
   "type": "inscription",
   "style": "scrawl",
   "wall": [
    [
     35,
     33
    ],
    "n"
   ],
   "caption": "Scratched into the wall above the bones",
   "title": "Scrawled in haste",
   "sig": "B.",
   "pages": [
    "THEY ONLY WAKE TO FLAME\nSHUTTER IT\nTEST THE FLOOR"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "burntText",
   "type": "inscription",
   "style": "look",
   "pos": [
    85400,
    80100
   ],
   "caption": "Bones on the floor",
   "title": "A scorched skeleton",
   "pages": [
    "A skeleton lies curled on its side, black with soot, still clutching a lantern with its shutters wide open. The flagstones around it have run like glass."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "plinthText",
   "type": "inscription",
   "style": "stele",
   "pos": [
    39600,
    68400
   ],
   "caption": "A plinth among the stone trees",
   "title": "The Garden of Bells",
   "pages": [
    "Three bells hang in my garden, poured in three different centuries.\n\nBronze is bright when it is young, and greens as the long years pass.\n\nWake them in the order they were poured, eldest first, or wake my gardeners instead."
   ]
  },
